+# Daily Grind phone verification
+
+Run `pnpm start` to serve this static app. The preview does not send SMS or verify real phone ownership. Enter a valid national phone number, then use **246810** to complete the demo. Codes expire after five minutes; resend is available after 30 seconds and resets the five-attempt limit.
+
+## Connecting SMS delivery
+
+Replace the `verification` adapter in `app.js` with requests to your backend. The server must generate random six-digit strings, send the SMS, enforce expiry, attempt and resend limits, and verify the code against a server-side challenge. Only report success after the server confirms verification. Remove the demo copy and hardcoded demo code when connecting the real provider.
+
+Never put SMS provider credentials or real OTP validation in client-side code. Bind the challenge to the phone number and the session, and invalidate it after successful use.
+
+For automatic extraction, serve over HTTPS and end your SMS with the exact host and code:
+
+```text
+Your Daily Grind verification code is 012345.
+
+@your-domain.example #012345
+```
+
+Use the hostname only, without protocol, port, or path. The WebOTP listener starts on the code step and on resend; it stops on submission, number changes, timeouts, and page exit. Unsupported browsers retain native `autocomplete="one-time-code"` suggestions and manual entry. The code is one labeled text input with a numeric keyboard so leading zeros, pasting, and screen readers work naturally.
